hadiths[40]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7200","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, dictating and reading, Ahmad bin Shayban Al-Ramli told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The most beloved drink to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sweet, cold.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, for it is not according to the Yemenis on the authority of Muammar.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7200 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7201","It was narrated to me by Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Yahya bin Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “He loved The drink was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sweet and cold.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7201 - Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Yahya Halak"
"7202","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Abdi narrated to us, Khalaf bin Al-Walid Al-Jawhari narrated to us, narrated to us Hushaym, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Saifi bin Suhaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the master “The drinks in this world and the hereafter are water.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7202 - True"
"7203","Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Abu Zubr Abdullah told us Ibn Al-Ala’ Ibn Zubr, Al-Dahhak Ibn Abd Al-Rahman Ibn Azab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings be upon him: “The first thing a servant will be held accountable on the Day of Resurrection will be said to him: Did I not cleanse your body for you and quench your thirst with cold water?” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7203 - True"
"7204","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to draw water for him.” “Fresh water from watering houses.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7204 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7205","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Nahwi told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir told us, Abu Muammar, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed told us, Abu Issam told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he breathed three times into the vessel and said: “He quenched, healed, and commanded.” Anas said: “And I breathed three times into the drink.” This is an authentic hadith. They did not include it with this addition, but rather agreed on the hadith of Thumamah on the authority of Anas who used to breathe into the vessel three times.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7205 - True"
"7206","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade breathing into a vessel and drinking from a waterskin.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they agreed on the hadith of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father regarding the prohibition. About breathing in a vessel """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7206 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7207","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Anas bin Iyad told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abd al-Rahman al-Dawsi, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “None of you should breathe into the vessel.” If he drinks from it, but if he wants to exhale, let him delay it and then exhale. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
 He told us
 Aban bin Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, Raised: “If one of you drinks, let him drink in one breath” according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7207 - True"
"7208","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa told us Al-Barti said: Al-Qanabi narrated to us, in what he read to Malik, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Habib, the client of Banu Zuhra, on the authority of Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Juhani, he said: I was sitting with Marwan bin Al-Hakam when Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, entered and Marwan said to him: “I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he forbids blowing on a drink? He said: Yes, and a man said to him: I cannot quench my thirst with one breath. He said: “Remove the vessel from your mouth and then breathe.” He said: So if you see dirt? He said: “Throw it away.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7208 - True"
"7209","Abu Abbas al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, he told me Abu Nahik, he said: I heard Amr ibn Akhtab say: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked for water, so I brought him water, and there was a hair in it, so I took it. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, make him beautiful.” He said: “I saw him when he was ninety-four years old, and there was no white hair on his head.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7209 - True"
"7210","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Sulayman al-Taymi told me, on the authority of al-Hasan Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with a stream of water and he knelt “In it while he was standing, he drank from it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7210 - Ali bin Asim Wah"
"7211","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade drinking from the waterskin because that “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7211 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7212","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Amir Al-Ghafari told us, Zamaa bin Salih told us, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the circumcision of waters. And after the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a man had forbidden him, he went out at night to a water-drinker and circumcised him, and a serpent came out of him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7212 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7213","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoob Al-Hafiz informed us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Musaddad told us, Ismail told us, he informed us Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade drinking from someone from a waterskin.” He said Ayoub: “Then I was informed that a man drank from the waterskin and a snake came out.” It is true according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not take it out.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7213 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7214","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi informed us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San’ani told us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Karim Abu Hisham told us Al-Sana’ani, Ibrahim bin Aqeel bin Maqil bin Munabbih told me, on the authority of his father Aqeel, on the authority of Wahb, he said: This is what I asked Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, and he told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: “Lean down the roofs and close the doors when you lie down.” At night, prepare the drink and food, for the devil will come. If he does not find the door closed, he will enter it, and if the watering can does not find a watering can, he will drink from it. And if he finds the door closed and the water-skin is propped up, he will not let him wait nor open a closed door, even if one of you does not find a vessel with which to brew it. So let him present a stick to him.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7214 - True"
"7215","Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Abdi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Harami bin Amara, Al-Harithi bin Al-Harith narrated to me, Ibn Abi Mulaika narrated to me, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “We used to put God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has three fermented vessels: a vessel for his ablution, a vessel for his siwak, and a vessel for his drinking. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7215 - True"
"7216","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Baladi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak Al-Souri told us, Yahya bin Hamza told us, Zaid bin Waqid narrated to me, that Khaled bin Abdullah bin Hussein, narrated to him, saying: Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks alcohol in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter. And whoever drinks from vessels of gold and silver in this world will not drink from it in the Hereafter.” Then he said: “The clothing of the people of Paradise and the drink of the people of Paradise.” “And the vessels of the people of Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7216 - True"
"7217","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of John ibn Qatada, on the authority of Salamah ibn Al-Muhabaq, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in The Battle of Tabuk He called for water from a woman, and she said: I have no water except for a dead skin of mine. He said: Haven’t you tanned it? She said: Yes. He said: “For she was slaughtered by her tanner.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7217 - True"
"7218","Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told me, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shaiban told us, about Al-Amash, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Raisins and dates are “Alcohol,” meaning if they all renounced it, “this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7218 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7219","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i informed us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Rabi’ah bin Kulthum bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father Kulthum bin Jubayr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “A prohibition was revealed. Alcohol in two tribes of the Ansar. They drank to the point that when they got drunk, they messed with each other. When they woke up, the man saw the effect. With his face, his head, and his beard, and he says: So-and-so did my brother, and by God, if He were compassionate and merciful to me, he would not have done this to me. He said: And they were “Brothers in whose hearts there are no grudges, yet grudges have taken place in their hearts.” So God Almighty revealed: “It is only wine and gambling” [Al-Ma’idah: 90] - to His saying - {So are you desisted?} [Al-Ma’idah: 91] “Then some of the hypocrites said: It is an abomination, and it is in the stomach of so-and-so who was killed on the day of Badr, and so-and-so was killed.” On the day of Uhud, then God Almighty revealed: {There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten} [Al-Ma’idah: 93] - until it was conveyed - {And God loves The doers of good.” [Al Imran: 134]
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7219 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7220","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Hassan narrated to us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari, Abu Abdullah al-Bushangi told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Waki` told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “A man from the Ansar called us before it was declared ihram.” Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came forward and led them in the Maghrib prayer and recited: “Say, ‘O you disbelievers,’ and he was confused about it.” Then it was revealed: {No. “Approach prayer while you are intoxicated” [An-Nisa: 43] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and there was disagreement about it regarding Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib from There are three aspects, this being the first and most correct.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7220 - True"
"7221","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, “that he and Abd al-Rahman and a man Others were drinking alcohol, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf led them in prayer. He recited: “Say, O you disbelievers.” So he mixed in it and it was revealed: “Do not approach the prayer.” And you are drunk.} [An-Nisa: 43]"
"7222","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Musaddad bin Mashad told us, Khaled bin Abdullah told us, about Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, that Abd al-Rahman made food. He said: “So he invited some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, among them. Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, recited: {Say, O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship} [Al-Kafirun: 2] And We worship what you worship. Then God Almighty revealed: “O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying” [An-Nisa: 43] “These are the chains of narrations.” All of them are authentic, and the ruling is based on the hadith of Sufyan Al-Thawri, for he has better memory than everyone who narrated it on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib.”"
"7223","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, about Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Maysara, on the authority of Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When he stood up for prayer, the caller of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: {No. “Approach prayer while you are intoxicated.” [An-Nisa: 43] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7223 - True"
"7224","Abu Yahya Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Samarqandi told me in Bukhara. Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Imam told us, Muhammad ibn Muammar, Humaid bin Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza, Hamza Al-Zayat told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib, he said: Omar said, May God be pleased with him: O God, make clear to us regarding wine, so the verse was revealed: {O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are drunk until you know what You say} [An-Nisa: 43] until the end of the verse, “So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Omar and he recited it to him,” as if it did not agree with what Omar wanted, so he said: O God, make clear to us regarding wine, so the verse was revealed: {They ask you about wine and gambling. Say, “In them is a great sin and benefits for the people, but their sin is greater.” Who will benefit them?} [Al-Baqarah: 219], “Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Omar and he recited it to him,” as if it did not agree with what Omar wanted, so he said: O God. Explain for us regarding wine, so it was revealed: {O you who have believed! Indeed, wine and gambling and the stones and the arrows are an abomination from the work of Satan. So avoid it} [Al-Maeda: 90] until he concluded by saying: {So are you desisted?} [Al-Maeda: 91] “So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called Omar and he recited it to him.” Omar said: We have finished, O Lord. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7224 - This is correct"
"7225","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Samak Ibn Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, they said: O Messenger of God, how? Our brothers who died drinking it? He said: So it was revealed: “There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten” [Al-Ma’idah: 93] “This verse” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7225 - True"
"7226","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad bin Al-Hasan Al-Awfi told us, Abi Saad bin Al-Hassan told us, Sulayman bin Qurm told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, the Jews said: Isn’t it Did your brothers who died drink it? Then God Almighty revealed: “There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have been fed” [Al-Maeda: 93], and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It was said to me: ‘You? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, rather they agreed on the hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of Abu Ishaq on the authority of Al-Bara’, summarizing this meaning.” """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7226 - True"
"7227","Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Nusayr al-Khalidi told us, Ahmad bin Bishr al-Murtadi told us, Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Muhammad al-Mubaraki told us, Abu Shihab Al-Hannat, Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi told us, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: “When the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked and greeted one another and said: Wine has been forbidden and has been made... Justice for polytheism: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7227 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7228","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Shurayh Al-Khawlani, that he had an uncle who sold alcohol and he used to give its price in charity, so I forbade him from doing so, but he did not stop, so I came In Medina, I met Ibn Abbas and asked him about wine and its price. He said: “It is forbidden and its price is forbidden.” Then he said: “O community of the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, if there had been a Book after your Book or a Prophet after your Prophet, it would have been revealed to you as it was revealed to those who were before you, but This will delay your affairs until the Day of Resurrection, and my life is more difficult for you.” He said: Then I met Abdullah bin Omar, and I asked him about the price. And he said: I will tell you about the wine. I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque, and while he was seeking his goal, he untied his bottle. Then he said: “Whoever has any wine, let him bring it to me.” So he made the people come to him, and one of them said, “I have a narrator of wine,” and the other said. I have a narrator, and the other says: I have Zaqiq, or whatever God wills that he has, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Gather him in such-and-such Baqi’.” And so on, then give me permission.” So they did so, then they called him to prayer. He said: So I got up and walked away while he was leaning on me. We followed Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took me. He greeted me and placed me on his left and put Abu Bakr in my place. Then Omar followed us and took me and placed me on his left. He walked between them until he stopped at The winemaker said to the people: “Do you know this?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, this wine. He said: “You are right.” Then he said: “Indeed, God Almighty has cursed wine and the one who presses it, the one who is pressing it, the one who drinks it, the servers of it, the one who carries it, and the one to whom it is carried.” He sold it to its buyer and ate its price. Then he called for a knife and said: “Sharpen it.” They did so, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it. He would pierce the alley with it, and the people said: There is a benefit in these alleys. So he said: “Yes, but I am only doing it to anger God because of His wrath in it.” Omar said: I am sufficient for you, O Messenger of God. He said: “No,” and some of them add more to each other in this hadith. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7228 - True"
"7229","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Malik bin Hussein Al-Zayadi told me, that Malik bin Saad Al-Tajibi told him that he heard Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Gabriel came to him.” Peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: O Muhammad, God has cursed wine and the one who presses it, the one who squeezes it, the one who carries it, the one to whom it is carried, the one who drinks it, and the one who sells it. And what she bought, her legs, and her drink: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7229 - True"
"7230","Abu Sahl Ziyad bin Al-Qattan told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Badal bin Al-Muhabbar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol in this world will not drink it in the hereafter.” This An authentic, strange hadith from the hadith of Shu’bah. The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith of Ubayd Allah bin Amr bin Jurayj on the authority of Nafi’ in This section """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7230 - Strange from the hadith of Shu’bah"
"7231","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, On the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Avoid “Alcohol is the key to all evil.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7231 - True"
"7232","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, about Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He drank wine and became intoxicated by it, his prayers would not be accepted for him for forty days. Then if he drank some of it until he became intoxicated by it, his prayers would not be accepted for him for forty days. Then if he drinks it and becomes intoxicated by it, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. Then if he drinks it the fourth time and becomes intoxicated by it, it is God’s duty to give him something to drink. From Ain Al-Khabal. It was said: What is Ain Al-Khabal? He said: “The pus of the people of Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7232 - True"
"7233","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told us, That Amr bin Al-Harith narrated to him, that Amr bin Shuaib narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever abandons prayer once intoxicated, it is as if he had the world and all that is in it and has been deprived of it. He left prayer four times because he was intoxicated. It was God Almighty’s obligation to give him to drink of the clay of the idle. It was said: What is the clay of the idle? He said: “The juice of the people of Hell.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7233 - Ibn Wahb heard it on his authority and it is very strange"
"7234","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, He said: I read from Al-Fudayl, on the authority of Abu Jarir, that Abu Burdah told him about the hadith of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “Three people will not enter Paradise: the alcoholic, the sever of ties of kinship, and the one who believes in magic, and whoever dies addicted to alcohol, God will give him to drink from a river.” Al-Ghouta “It was said: What is the Al-Ghouta River? He said: “A river emerges from the private parts of prostitutes, harming the people of Hell with the smell of their private parts.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7234 - True"
"7235","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, my brother told me, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Bilal, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Yasar Al-Araj, that he heard Salim, speaking on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Three God will not look at them on the Day of Resurrection: He who was disobedient to his parents, addicted to alcohol, and ungrateful for what he gave. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7235 - True"
"7236","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Al-Darawardi told me, Dawud bin Salih told me, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, and Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them, and some of the Companions of the Messenger of God They sat after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they mentioned the greatest sins, but they had no knowledge of them to conclude. So they sent me to Abdullah bin Amr, to ask him about that, and he told me that the greatest of sins is drinking alcohol, so I went to them. So I informed them, but they denied it and all jumped to him until they came to his house, and he informed them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of the kings of the children of Israel took a man and gave him a choice between drinking wine, killing a person, committing adultery, or eating meat.” The pig or they will kill him if he refuses and chooses to drink alcohol, and when he drank it he did not abstain from anything they wanted from him.” And that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us in answer: “There is no one who drinks it and God accepts his prayers for forty nights and he does not die with some of it in his bladder.” Nothing but Paradise will be forbidden to him thereby, and if he dies in forty nights, he will die a death of pre-Islamic times.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7236 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7237","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Saeed Bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muslim, that Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani performed Hajj and visited Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted her, and she began to ask him about Damascus and its cold, so he began to tell her, and she said: How can they be patient with its cold? He said: O Mother of the Believers, they are drinking a drink called tala. She said: God has spoken the truth and my love, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has conveyed. I heard him say: “Indeed, people from my nation drink alcohol and call it by another name.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7237 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7238","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Al-Mughirah Al-Saadi informed us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maryam bint Tariq, a woman from his people, said: I was among some of the immigrant women who performed Hajj. So we went to Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her. She said: So the women started asking her about the circumstances. She said: O women, you remember circumstances, many of which existed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so fear God and avoid Whatever intoxicates you, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden, but if it intoxicates the water of its seeds, then you should avoid it.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7238 - True"
"7239","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ubayy told us, and Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, they said: We told us: Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Khalid bin Katheer Al-Hamdani, narrated to him that Al-Sari bin Ismail Al-Kufi, narrated to him that Al-Sha’abi, He told him that he heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, of the wheat is wine and of the barley Wine, and wine from raisins, and wine from dates, and wine from honey, and I forbid you from every intoxicant.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “The Last Book of Drinks”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7239 - The secret they left behind"
